🧱 Key Architectural Components
AI Coding Agent (MCP Client): High-level orchestrator (Cursor, Claude Code, Windsurf) holding code context and UI test objectives.

Maestro MCP Server (maestro mcp): Standardized interface exposing agentic tools:

inspect_screen: Extracts compact JSON view hierarchy & bounding boxes.

run: Executes on-the-fly inline YAML commands without code compilation.

take_screenshot: Captures visual frame for visual disambiguation.

Target Runtime (Device/Simulator): Black-box host running the app release build.

Deterministic Output: Generates human-readable, maintainable Maestro YAML test flows for CI/CD pipeline integration.

🔄 Step-by-Step Closed Agentic Loop Workflow
Context & Intent: Developer asks the AI Agent to build a new feature or create/fix a UI test.

Screen Inspection: AI Agent invokes inspect_screen via MCP to inspect accessibility nodes and UI states on the active emulator.

Action Execution: AI Agent formats Maestro commands (tapOn, inputText, assertVisible) and calls run over stdio/JSON-RPC.

Self-Healing & Iteration: If an assertion fails or element is missing, the AI Agent re-inspects the hierarchy, self-corrects selectors/code, and re-tests.

YAML Export: Once validated, the AI Agent saves a clean, deterministic .yaml flow into source control for CI/CD execution.

💡 Architectural Takeaway
AI is the test engineer and executor in a local loop via MCP, but the final artifact delivered to CI/CD is a fast, 100% deterministic YAML file.

📄 SLIDE 2: Scenario 2 Architecture – Testing In-App AI Agents using Maestro
Slide Title: Architecture: Validating In-App AI Agents with Maestro
Subtitle: End-to-End Assertion of Non-Deterministic AI Interfaces & Dynamic UI Workflows
🎨 Visual Architecture Diagram
Plaintext
  +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
  |                             TEST AUTOMATION ENVIRONMENT                           |
  |                                                                                   |
  |   +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+   |
  |   |                            Maestro Test Runner                            |   |
  |   |  - YAML Flow (`launchApp`, `inputText`, `assertWithAI`, `extendedWait`)   |   |
  |   |  - GraalJS Script Engine (`http.get`, dynamic parsing, status checking)   |   |
