  |   |                     SYSTEM UNDER TEST (SUT) MOBILE APP                    |   |
  |   |                                                                           |   |
  |   |   +---------------------+   App Network    +--------------------------+   |   |
  |   |   |  App UI / Chat Bot  |=================>|  Backend AI / LLM Agent  |   |   |
  |   |   | (Streaming Response)|   Requests/WebSock|  (API Mock or Live LLM)  |   |   |
  |   |   +---------------------+                  +--------------------------+   |   |
  |   +---------------------------------------------------------------------------+   |
  +-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
                                            |
                                            v Visual & Semantic Audit
                             +-------------------------------+
                             |  Maestro Cloud AI Analysis    |
                             |  (`assertWithAI` LLM Layer)   |
                             +-------------------------------+
🧱 Key Architectural Components
System Under Test (SUT): The actual release build containing an embedded conversational agent or generative UI.

Maestro Driver Layer: Tests app externally using OS Accessibility APIs (no app instrumentation required).

extendedWaitUntil & Dynamic Matchers: Native Maestro mechanics handling asynchronous streaming responses and non-deterministic text generation.

Semantic & Visual Assertion Layer (assertWithAI / assertNoDefectsWithAI): Maestro Cloud LLM evaluation layer verifying context, intent, and layout without strict exact-string matching.

Backend Mocking / Deterministic Seeds: Optional Mock/Stub layer on network calls to stabilize LLM outputs during CI runs.

🔄 Step-by-Step Test Execution Workflow
Trigger Agent: Maestro inputs user prompts/intents into the app's chat input (inputText).

Handle Non-Determinism & Streaming: Maestro waits for AI activity indicators (e.g., typing indicators, loading spinners) using extendedWaitUntil.

Semantic UI Assertion: Since exact AI responses vary across runs, Maestro utilizes assertWithAI to semantically validate that the AI answer fulfills the requirement (e.g., "Verify the AI generated a valid order confirmation table").

UI Safety & Layout Check: assertNoDefectsWithAI scans for layout breaks, text overflows, or broken dynamic widgets generated by the LLM response.

💡 Architectural Takeaway
Maestro treats the app's internal AI as a black box—using flexible timing, regex/semantic assertions (assertWithAI), and external driver actions to test unpredictable app responses.
